  "Question": "When the common ratio is \\(q=1\\), why can't we directly use \\(S_n=a_1(q^n-1)/(q-1)\\)?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "A sequence with a common ratio of 1 does not exist",
    "B": "The first term must be 0",
    "C": "The denominator is 0",
    "D": "The number of terms must be infinite"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(q-1=0\\), so the denominator makes the formula undefined. Use \\(S_n=na_1\\) instead.",
